@Maya @Carlos @Samir @Inez @Lena @Raj I updated the working doc with one concrete rule for mid‑retry user actions: if the user taps "Try again" while the backend is still within the active retry window for the same paymentAttemptId, the client will attach to the in‑flight attempt (keep showing "Processing…", do not create a new attempt) and surface that attempt’s final result; only if the in‑flight attempt returns a terminal failure or exceeds the retry window will the user's retry create a new paymentAttemptId and start a fresh attempt. 

Finalized end‑to‑end summary to copy into #eng‑payments: use idempotent paymentAttemptId; auto‑retry on network timeouts/gateway 5xx up to 2 attempts with exponential backoff (~0.5s then ~2s) within a 30s window; allow at most 1 auto‑retry for gateway‑advised soft declines within 30s; never auto‑retry on hard declines; client shows "Processing…" during retries, confirmation on success, "Temporary issue — Try again" (manual CTA) for soft/gateway errors, and "Card declined" with update steps for hard declines; QA/ops notes (retry caps, retries_exhausted metric, and full QA matrix) are in the doc. 

Please review and flag any objections here before tomorrow’s sync.
